# Allow and deny a tool

## Section

The Agent declares `multiply`. One request permits it. The next request
narrows access with `allowed_tools: []`. The mock script makes the offered
tool set easy to inspect. Change `backend` to `:live` and set
`OPENAI_API_KEY` to see how a real model behaves with each request.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:tools, [%{id: "allowed", name: "multiply", arguments: %{a: 2, b: 3}}]}},
  %{reply: {:text, "The product is 6."}},
  %{reply: {:text, "I cannot use a tool for this request."}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)
context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Declare the tool

```elixir
defmodule Guide.PolicyMultiply do
  use Jido.Action,
    name: "guide_policy_multiply",
    schema: Zoi.object(%{a: Zoi.integer(), b: Zoi.integer()})

  @impl Jido.Action
  def run(%{a: a, b: b}, _context), do: {:ok, %{value: a * b}}
end

defmodule Guide.ToolPolicy do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_tool_policy"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("")})

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      reasoning :react

      tools do
        action Guide.PolicyMultiply, as: :multiply
      end

      controls do
        timeout 15_000
        max_model_calls 2
        max_tool_calls 1
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.tool_policy", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Ask with two access levels

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.ToolPolicy, id: "guide-tool-policy")

{:ok, allowed} = Guide.ToolPolicy.ask_sync(server, "Use multiply for 2 times 3.", context: context)

{:ok, narrowed} =
  Guide.ToolPolicy.ask_sync(server, "Can you use multiply now?",
    context: context,
    allowed_tools: []
  )

%{with_tool: allowed, without_tool: narrowed}
```

Mock mode has three provider requests: tool choice, tool continuation, and
the narrowed request. Inspect the last request's offered tools.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [first, _, last]} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
  %{first_tools: first.body["tools"], narrowed_tools: last.body["tools"]}
end
```

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Tool access and effects](../v3/14_tool_policy.md).
